{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202112-quitting-an-order-for-another","id":1202112,"title":"Quitting an Order for another","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-01T20:05:40-07:00","id":1202112,"title":"Quitting an Order for another","content":"So... My wife has made here character and she wants to have her character be a former member of the the Silver Ladder who became disillusioned by the actions of her first Mentor and leave and join the Free Council.<br /> <br /> So here's my question. If she was allowed to do this, would she have the rote specialties for both Orders? I know the answer for 1st edition. Looking for a 2nd edition answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:22:33-07:00","id":1202113,"title":"","content":"I don't think she would at base, but you could allow it as a merit, similar to how nameless orders gain rotespecialties through merits (usually as a part of their mystery cult initiation). I'd say 1 merit point per rote skill (so 3 for the full set).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:54:24-07:00","id":1202120,"title":"","content":"I'd say she could buy them the same way you purchase any specialty, which is 1 XP per if I remember correctly. Alternatively, you could allow her to exchange the Rote Specialties from the SL for the ones from the FC as indoctrination in one Order overwrites the indoctrination and training from the other Order. Either way, it's a decent story hook/complication, to have some kind of inhibition for her to share former Rote Specialties from one Order to the other, like a severe Oath or something. She's probably also burned quite a few bridges with the SL and can have problems interacting with them in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:57:03-07:00","id":1202121,"title":"","content":"I'd say no. Rote specialties are about more than just &quot;this Order likes Rotes that use these Skills&quot;; an Order has its rote specialties because those activities are metaphysically aligned with that Order's symbolism. When you leave one Order to join another, you're aligning yourself with a different set of symbols - especially leaving a Diamond Order for the Free Council, which shares so little doctrine or symbolism with the others - so even if you still know the Rotes you were previously taught, you no longer get that added bit of metaphorical juice that comes along with belonging to an ancient mystical Order who's ethos resonates with the symbolism of its Mudras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24025-fourgigsofdurnk","name":"Fourgigsofdurnk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T21:32:25-07:00","id":1202124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fourgigsofdurnk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202112-quitting-an-order-for-another?p=1202121#post1202121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially leaving a Diamond Order for the Free Council, which shares so little doctrine or symbolism with the others</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's a fine interpretation of the rules, I'd argue this particular point in terms of rp execution. All six Orders have an intentional degree of overlap in their philosophies or actions. Give me any two Orders and I can tell you where they can find common ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-02-2018, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T21:45:42-07:00","id":1202127,"title":"","content":"Perhaps start off with Silver Ladder rote specialties, then swap Expression and Subterfuge for Crafts and Science when the character finally connects with Libertine Creed, leaving behind the Elemental Precepts<br /> Or, have her already have arrived at that point.<br /> <br /> I don't like devaluing Order rote specialties as just something you can 'buy' when you swap between Orders.<br /> The Orders are mystic engines that draw symbolic strength from their creed and principles, and their rote specialties are a big part of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T03:29:40-07:00","id":1202180,"title":"","content":"No, you can only have one set of three. If you're in an Order they come with membership and training, if you're Nameless you get to buy them.<br /> <br /> Mages who learn a new set find it pushes the old set out.<br /> <br /> You do, however, keep any special Order Merits you had, although IIRC there's a cap on how much Status you can have in an Order that isn't your own. A Seer with Prelacy who defects doesn't lose Prelacy, for example.<br /> <br /> Most Orders are grudgingly accepting of &quot;career changes&quot; in younger (lower status) mages, but are much less happy the more senior you are. Quitting when at the top means social exclusion and noticably more duelling challenges and other frictions, and that's if another Order will even decide it's worth pissing their allies off enough to accept them. You can go Nameless, but that's even more isolating.<br /> <br /> This kind of thing is why the Orders are happy to give someone senior a desk job, shuffle them off into no duties, or in the Arrow's case run an entire Nameless Order (the Vidanti) *inside* the Arrow specifically for people who can't follow their tenets any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}